module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_dedicated_worker_meets_owner_assumptions_made_for_a_service_user_worker

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_dedicated_worker_meets_owner_assumptions_made_for_a_service_user_worker: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_dedicated_worker_meets_owner_assumptions_made_for_a_service_user_worker" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: MechanicallyPreventable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "a handed-set entry that carries the principal who reads or writes it, from which every directory mode, file grant, custody location and git trust the worker unit is given is derived for each WorkerIdentity arm, sufficient for a path handed to a WorkerDedicatedAccount unit with no access derived for that account to refuse when the spawn is planned rather than when the worker first touches it" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a path the worker unit reads or writes was made, located or owned on the assumption that the worker IS the instance service user (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance WorkerIsServiceUser), and the unit runs as a dedicated account (WorkerDedicatedAccount: user gunbc-worker, group gunbc-attempt) that is neither its owner nor has a home.",
    "RECEIPTS, srv1 lab on bright-moth-475/lab-dev, 2026-10-21 to 2026-10-25, each found by the next real attempt failing one step further: (b) the attempt directory installed 0700, refused at the worker-traversal step (#15007); (c) the first harness turn refused reading /nonexistent/.config/... because the route's key is custody under HOME and the account has no home (lab-dev 77ff833e: LoadCredential= from a root credstore copy); (d) provider-events.jsonl and the wire directory made owner-only, refused at the first round (lab-dev 9db359e9, on main via #15007); (e) every git call refused with detected dubious ownership, since `git worktree add` runs as the service user (lab-dev 4232080f: safe.directory for the one worktree through the environment); (f) 851 of 852 checkout directories and all 10362 files without group write, so the model edited nothing (lab-dev 60438c67: the worktree grant and its refusal walk).",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: each failure names a path and a permission or ownership refusal; the same layout passes for WorkerIsServiceUser (srv1 live); the unit's handed set (gunbc.roadmap.dispatch_worker_handed_set) names the path but carries no fact about which principal reads or writes it, so each mode was decided at its own creation site.",
    "HARM: an attempt that cannot run, or runs for hours and produces nothing usable (receipt f: two hours, 121 rounds, no edit landed). Each instance was loud, not silent, because the worker's refusal named the path.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the refusals on the host). CURRENT RUNG: mechanically preventable, per instance: claims pin the dedicated-account arm of each fixed site (test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_traversal_witness the_dedicated_worker_unit_loads_the_route_key_from_the_root_credstore; test.claim.roadmap.attempt_system_unit_launch_witness the_dedicated_worker_starts_trusting_only_its_own_worktree; test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator_witness the_dedicated_worker_worktree_grant_sweeps_then_proves_and_never_touches_the_pointer, the_dedicated_worker_attempt_directory_is_group_traversable_and_its_scratch_group_writable), and the spawn refuses before the unit starts on an ungranted checkout (the refusal walk) or an untraversable chain. A NEW path added with a service-user assumption is still writable and is found by the next lab attempt.",
    "NEIGHBOUR: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_foreign_uid_is_handed_a_path_it_cannot_reach_or_a_manager_creates_one_its_consumer_cannot_use owns the two links this row does not: an ANCESTOR the foreign uid cannot traverse (receipt a of the same lab run, 200/CHDIR on .local/share) and a path the MANAGER creates for a consumer. This row is the worker's own leaves: what it reads (a credential located under the owner's HOME), writes (an owner-only directory or stream, a checkout the owner made under its umask) or runs git in (a repository git trusts only for its owner). Both are instances of one root, the worker identity changing while each site kept the old one, and the standing's trigger is that root's construction.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Which principal enters a path is decidable from the instance's WorkerIdentity and the path's role, so a handed set carrying the accessor can derive every mode and refuse a path with no derivation. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the accessor-carrying handed-set entry named in the standing. Residual outside the guarantee: the host's real ownership is observed only by the traversal step and the refusal walk at spawn.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
